      "info": {
        "title": "3ds-recorder",
        "author": "BolgarMaxym97",
        "description": "Record your whole Nintendo 3DS screen — games, HOME Menu and apps, both screens with sound — with a Luma3DS sysmodule. Converts recordings to MP4 on the console and sends them to your phone over Wi-Fi via QR code. Old & New 3DS.",
        "category": [
          "homebrew"
        ],
        "console": [
          "3DS"
        ],
        "version": "v0.11.4-beta",
        "license": "MIT",
        "last_updated": "2026-11-10 at 04:49 (UTC)",
        "releasenotes": "v0.11.4-beta (2026-11-10)\n> [!WARNING]\n> Beta. Tested on an Old 3DS with Luma3DS 13.5. The New 3DS changes in this release (faster processor while recording, new compression, 800 px mode) have not been tested on a New 3DS yet. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new in 0.11.4\n\n- Both screens stay smooth when the SD card is the limit. In 3D games the card can't take every frame of both screens. The bottom screen used to pause then; now it slows down a little first and the top keeps its full rate. Mario Kart 7 on an Old 3DS: about 22 fps on top and 11 below, steady, with no lost frames.\n- Better sound: the recorder now sleeps between frames instead of waking up every 2 ms, which leaves the system core to the game. The longest gap in sound polling went from about 0.2 s to under 7 ms.\n- Faster SD writes (bigger write blocks, the recorder's SD access at low priority so the game's own loading comes first) and less wasted space in recordings.\n- Settings → Screens → Bottom: record only the bottom screen, for games played there.\n- Games that need extra memory on an Old 3DS (Smash, Pokémon Sun / Moon…): about 9% more of the SD bandwidth goes to the video.\n- New 3DS: the processor runs at 804 MHz with the L2 cache while recording (back as it was afterwards), frames that change all over are compressed much better, a bigger buffer rides out slow SD cards, and games using the 800 px...\n\n----------\n\nv0.9.14-beta (2026-11-08)\n> [!WARNING]\n> Beta. Tested on an Old 3DS and a New 3DS XL with Luma3DS 13.5, but bugs are possible. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new in 0.9.14\n\n- Smoother recordings on an Old 3DS. Encoding now runs on the game's own processor core at the lowest priority, using only the time the game leaves idle, instead of competing with the game on the system core. In Mario Kart 7 a 103-second recording of both screens lost only 36 frames; in Smash, encoding is about twice as fast. New 3DS is unchanged.\n- In games that need extra memory on an Old 3DS (Smash, Pokémon Sun / Moon…), the video is still limited by memory there: for smoother video record only the top screen (Settings → Screens → Top). The help and README say so.\n- The panel showed the wrong version (0.9.11) in 0.9.12–0.9.13; fixed.\n\nEverything from 0.9.13 is included: games that need extra memory on an Old 3DS (Smash Bros, Pokémon Sun / Moon and Ultra Sun / Ultra Moon, Super Mario Maker, Monster Hunter) can be recorded, through a tiny launcher plugin for Luma's plugin loader.\n\nInstall: 3ds-recorder.cia with FBI (or 3ds-recorder.3dsx in /3ds/ for the Homebrew Launcher). In the Luma menu (hold SELECT at power-on) turn on Enable loading external FIRMs and modules. Open 3DS Recorder; R + SELECT starts and stops a recording. Updating: install over the old version and open the app once. Details:...\n\n----------\n\nv0.9.13-beta (2026-11-08)\n> [!WARNING]\n> Beta. Tested on an Old 3DS and a New 3DS XL with Luma3DS 13.5, but bugs are possible. If something goes wrong, please open an issue and attach the log (phone page → Log for the developer, or /3ds/recorder/app.log and recorder.log from the SD card).\n\nWhat's new in 0.9.13\n\n- Games that need extra memory on an Old 3DS can be recorded now: Smash Bros, Pokémon Sun / Moon and Ultra Sun / Ultra Moon, Super Mario Maker, Monster Hunter. These games restart the console when they start; the recorder comes back inside the game by itself and a running recording goes on in a new file. It works through a tiny launcher plugin for Luma's plugin loader (about 1 KB, it only starts the recorder again); if the plugin loader is off, it is turned on just for that game. The HOME Menu works during the recording as without the recorder. When such a game closes, the recording is saved and the app explains what happened.\n- On an Old 3DS the video in these games is less smooth (the console has little power and memory to spare there). New 3DS and other games are unchanged.\n- New help topic and README section about these games.\n\nInstall: 3ds-recorder.cia with FBI (or 3ds-recorder.3dsx in /3ds/ for the Homebrew Launcher). In the Luma menu (hold SELECT at power-on) turn on Enable loading external FIRMs and modules. Open 3DS Recorder; R + SELECT starts and stops a recording. Updating from 0.9.0: install over it and open the app once. Details: README.\n\n---\n\n> Бета. Перевірено на Old 3DS і New 3D...",
        "wiki": "https://github.com/BolgarMaxym97/3ds-recorder"
      }
    },
